make('tentoki-and-ryutoki','Tentōki and Ryūtōki, the two small oni-shaped Buddhist offering guardians','Exactly TWO small oni-shaped living figures, each one head, two eyes, two arms and two legs, compact fierce faces, fully covered in plain opaque short robes. Tentōki on left supports one large unlettered lantern on left shoulder and hand. Ryūtōki on right carries one lantern on head, a single long serpentine dragon coils around his body, hands crossed before body.','Tentōki leans forward under his lantern while Ryūtōki braces feet and looks upward, the coiled dragon lifts its head toward viewer; lantern-bearing pair confront from low angle.','No magical effect; physical lantern flame illuminates protective oni pair, not destructive demons.','Deep dark interior associated with Kōfuku-ji in Nara, only plain shadowed timber and stone.',(['tentoki-and-ryutoki-c01','tentoki-and-ryutoki-c02','tentoki-and-ryutoki-c04','tentoki-and-ryutoki-c06','tentoki-and-ryutoki-c07'],['tentoki-and-ryutoki-c03'],['tentoki-and-ryutoki-c04','tentoki-and-ryutoki-c06']),'Animate the documented iconographic pair rather than render museum statues. Respectful protective awe; no invented giant scale.', 'Extreme low angle close view; both faces and distinct lantern positions remain clearly visible. Small oni proportions.')
